      ],
      "explanation": "Since \\(20=4\\cdot5\\), finding the fourth powers lets us avoid expanding twentieth powers. Using \\(i^2=-1\\),\n\\[\n(1+i)^2=1+2i+i^2=2i,\n\\qquad\n(1-i)^2=1-2i+i^2=-2i.\n\\]\nSquaring again gives\n\\[\n(1+i)^4=(2i)^2=-4,\n\\qquad\n(1-i)^4=(-2i)^2=-4.\n\\]\nThus both twentieth powers equal \\((-4)^5=-1024\\). Their difference is therefore \\(0\\), choice C.",
      "id": "equal-fourth-powers",
